choice("Suggest calling Rose on the transceiver so she can freeze time for thirty seconds.", B3-Ch06a-Rose-Asleep, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06a-Rose-Asleep, v_b3_ch6_plan = 3) if (v_b3_ch6_sleep == 1 && v_b3_ch6_survey == 0 || v_b3_ch6_sleep == 1 && v_b3_ch6_survey == 1)


ID: B3-Ch06a-Hadrik-Plan
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_aura_hardening >= 2 || v_combat_technique >= 1)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_aura_hardening < 2 && v_combat_technique < 1)
#if(v_b3_ch6_plan == 0 && v_combat_technique >= 1) {
"Melindra's wind control is too volatile," I say on the run. "Holding the barrier yesterday doesn't guarantee stability today. Let Hadrik draw the initial volley."

"Keep moving," Hadrik says, his teeth bared in a wild grin. "I'll turn these flying kettles into scrap."

His stout form shrinks, golden feathers sprouting along his arms as he shifts into a massive eagle. He launches upward with a screech, cutting into the lead formation. Ten feet above the rooftops he snaps back to dwarven shape mid-air, drives a heavy leather boot into the optic lens of the nearest sphere, and sends the shattered hull spinning into the masonry below.

"Why encourage him?" Kate mutters as we sprint through the alley mouth. "He can't hold fifty of them alone."

"He doesn't have to," I say. "He absorbs punishment better than the rest of us combined. He shatters the front rank, and we handle the spillover."

"The spillover is thirty drones," Kate says.

As Kate warns, the swarm computes Hadrik's lone disruption, delegates three units to pin him, and routes the main swarm straight at our sprinting line.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_plan == 0 && v_combat_technique < 1) {
"Melindra's wind control is too volatile," I say on the run. "Holding the barrier yesterday doesn't guarantee stability today. Let Hadrik draw the initial volley."

"Keep moving," Hadrik says, his teeth bared in a wild grin. "I'll turn these flying kettles into scrap."

His stout form shrinks, golden feathers sprouting along his arms as he shifts into a massive eagle. He launches upward with a screech, cutting into the lead formation. Ten feet above the rooftops he snaps back to dwarven shape mid-air, drives a heavy leather boot into the optic lens of the nearest sphere, and sends the shattered hull spinning into the masonry below.

"Why encourage him?" Kate mutters as we sprint through the alley mouth. "He can't hold fifty of them alone."

"He doesn't have to," I say. "He absorbs punishment better than the rest of us combined. He shatters the front rank, and we handle the spillover."

"The spillover is thirty drones," Kate says.

As Kate warns, the swarm computes Hadrik's lone disruption, delegates three units to pin him, and routes the main swarm straight at our sprinting line.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_plan == 2 && v_combat_technique >= 1) {
As Kate warns, the swarm computes Hadrik's lone disruption, delegates three units to pin him, and routes the main swarm straight at our sprinting line.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_plan == 2 && v_combat_technique < 1) {
As Kate warns, the swarm computes Hadrik's lone disruption, delegates three units to pin him, and routes the main swarm straight at our sprinting line.

}
A wall of bronze spheres drops into the lane fifty paces ahead, red lenses glowing as energy crackles across their weapon ports.

"Clear a corridor," Daren shouts, drawing sword and shield, his scar tightening. "Form up!"

"No," I say. "You and Kelrim push through. Take Hadrik to punch through the line. We pull the swarm into the air and keep their guns off you."

"Kelrim is our only navigator!" Daren yells over the rising whine of turbines. "You'll lose us in the district!"

"We track you from above," I say. "Melindra can lock your aura. Move! Hadrik, carve a hole for Daren!"

Hadrik drops from a roof ledge in dwarf form, smashing two spheres together with a deafening clang. Daren, Kelrim, and Hadrik bull-rush through the breach toward the apothecary door.

Melindra flicks her fingers. Rushing air curls tight around my boots, lifting me ten feet off the flagstones. Flower ignites twin jets of orange flame beneath her bare heels, soaring alongside Kate, who rides a rising stair of frost. Leila stays low, daggers flashing as she intercepts low-altitude sweepers with lethal speed.

I unlimber my crossbow, cocking the stirrup with one smooth pull and snapping a steel bolt into the groove.

#if(v_combat_technique >= 1) {
My combat technique training keeps the chaotic crossfire readable. I track the micro-rotations of the bronze casings, anticipating discharge angles before the beams fire. In the air beside me, Flower unleashes crackling firebolts while Kate skewers optics with high-velocity ice shards. Below, Leila's silver daggers sever propulsion housings before the drones can stabilize.

We grind down their frontline until the surviving spheres break formation and retreat in a high climbing bank.

Down the avenue, Daren, Kelrim, and Hadrik emerge from Pete's storefront, satchels slung across their shoulders. We drop out of the sky to meet them on the cobblestones.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening >= 2 && v_combat_technique < 1) {
The swarm overwhelms my field of view. A bronze sphere drops from a blind angle behind my shoulder, its condenser whining as it discharges a direct lightning bolt into my back.

The shock slams into my spine, but my hardened aura and lessathi electrical resistance absorb the fatal surge. Pain burns along my ribs, but my fingers hold the trigger. I spin mid-air and drill a crossbow bolt straight through the drone's glowing red eye. The sphere detonates in a shower of copper shavings.

The remaining drones register the casualty rate, break formation, and retreat in a high climbing bank.

Down the avenue, Daren, Kelrim, and Hadrik emerge from Pete's storefront, satchels slung across their shoulders. We drop out of the sky to meet them on the cobblestones.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening < 2 && v_combat_technique < 1) {
The swarm overwhelms my field of view. A bronze sphere drops from a blind angle behind my shoulder, its condenser whining as it discharges a direct lightning bolt into my back.

The electric surge bypasses my thin defenses, roasting my flesh and nerves in an instant. My lungs seize. The crossbow slips from numb fingers. The cobblestones rush up to meet me, and darkness swallows the street.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06a-Entrance, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06a-Entrance) if (v_aura_hardening >= 2 || v_combat_technique >= 1)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_aura_hardening < 2 && v_combat_technique < 1)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_aura_hardening < 2 && v_combat_technique < 1)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_aura_hardening < 2 && v_combat_technique < 1)


ID: B3-Ch06a-Rose-Awake
TEXT:

"Rose can buy us a lane," I say. "If she halts time for thirty seconds like yesterday, we can reach the threshold without firing a shot."

"She nearly collapsed holding that spell yesterday," Kate says sharply. "I won't risk her health when we have steel and magic on the field."

"Even fifteen seconds breaks their net," I say. "I'll tell her to drop the anchor the moment she feels strain. Hold on."

I unclip the transceiver, spin the dial to Rose's rune, and tap the plate.

"Rose? Are you by the line?"

"I'm here," Rose's voice answers over the soft sizzle of a skillet. "What is it?"

"We have a swarm of mechanical sentinels boxing our street," I say.

"Sentinels?" Rose sounds puzzled. "What sentinels?"

"No time to explain," I say. "Can you lock time across the district, excluding our party? You don't need a full half-minute—fifteen seconds gives us an open door."

Silence stretches over the line.

"Rose? Are you weaving the field, or—"

The roar of drone thrusters cuts off instantly. The bronze spheres freeze motionless in mid-air, suspended against the gray sky like pinned insects. The whole city falls dead still.

"We have it!" I tell the device. "Keep the thread steady for ten more—"

The hum of turbines snarls back to life. Above us, the spheres bank and dive, the spell snapping apart after barely three seconds.

"I'm sorry!" Rose's voice trembles through the speaker. "I'm so sorry... my head is pounding, and the threads kept slipping through my fingers."

"Don't apologize," I say. "We woke you after an hour of rest. The fault is mine. Get back to the stove and rest. We'll handle the rest."

"Be careful!"

I slap the transceiver shut and pocket it on the run. "The net is still live. Plan B."

"On it!" Hadrik shouts. "Keep moving!"

His form shrinks, golden feathers sprouting along his arms as he shifts into a massive eagle. He launches upward, shrieking into the lead formation. Ten feet above the rooftops he snaps back to dwarven shape, drives a heavy leather boot into the optic lens of the nearest sphere, and sends it spinning into the masonry below.

"Why encourage him?" Kate mutters as we sprint through the alley mouth. "He can't hold fifty of them alone."

"He doesn't have to," I say. "He absorbs punishment better than the rest of us combined. He shatters the front rank, and we handle the spillover."

"The spillover is thirty drones," Kate says.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch06a-Hadrik-Plan, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06a-Hadrik-Plan)

ID: B3-Ch06a-Kate-Plan
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_aura_hardening >= 3 || v_combat_technique >= 2)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_aura_hardening < 3 && v_combat_technique < 2)
#if(v_combat_technique >= 2) {
"Kate's right, Hadrik," I say. "Her ice bursts clear wide arcs in the air. We need area control, not single punches."

"Fine," Hadrik grunts, angling toward the front with his axe loose in his grip. "I'll clear the ground-level scrap."

"Melindra, with me," Kate says, stamping her boot to summon a flat disc of solid blue ice over the flagstones.

Melindra frowns down at the rising disc. "My air currents are erratic today. I cannot guarantee a stable barrier under heavy bombardment."

"Step onto the frost," Kate says, her voice hard. "We adapt as we climb."

Melindra steps onto the platform. The ice disc lifts vertically on howling frost plumes, carrying them twenty feet into the crossfire.

"Keep your legs moving!" Daren shouts, shielding Kelrim with his armored shoulder.

I glance upward as we sprint. The bronze spheres converge on the rising platform, discharging crackling elemental lances. Melindra's wind barrier bends and flickers under the assault, buffeted by lightning arcs and kinetic slugs. The gale shudders on the verge of total collapse.

}
#if(v_combat_technique < 2) {
"Kate's right, Hadrik," I say. "Her ice bursts clear wide arcs in the air. We need area control, not single punches."

"Fine," Hadrik grunts, angling toward the front with his axe loose in his grip. "I'll clear the ground-level scrap."

"Melindra, with me," Kate says, stamping her boot to summon a flat disc of solid blue ice over the flagstones.

Melindra frowns down at the rising disc. "My air currents are erratic today. I cannot guarantee a stable barrier under heavy bombardment."

"Step onto the frost," Kate says, her voice hard. "We adapt as we climb."

Melindra steps onto the platform. The ice disc lifts vertically on howling frost plumes, carrying them twenty feet into the crossfire.

"Keep your legs moving!" Daren shouts, shielding Kelrim with his armored shoulder.

I glance upward as we sprint. The bronze spheres converge on the rising platform, discharging crackling elemental lances. Melindra's wind barrier bends and flickers under the assault, buffeted by lightning arcs and kinetic slugs. The gale shudders on the verge of total collapse.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening >= 3 && v_combat_technique < 2) {
"Daren, push for the shop," I call out. "Flower and I are backing them up. That barrier is about to crack."

"Petal and I are airborne!" Flower shouts, twin jets of orange flame flaring from her bare heels.

"Keep your visual on our line!" Daren bellows over the gunfire. "Kelrim is the only one with the street map!"

"Understood!" I yell up to the rooftops. "Melindra! Give me the updraft!"

Melindra flicks her wrist. Rushing wind curls tight beneath my boots, hurling me thirty feet into the sky. I unlimber my crossbow, nocking a heavy quarrel as Flower and I close ranks with Kate's ice platform.

Dozens of bronze spheres swivel toward us, their red lenses burning with malice. I cock and fire, dropping two drones through their optics, but fresh reinforcements peel off the cloud deck to replace them.

The sheer volume of fire blinds my peripheral vision. A drone drops silently out of the sun behind my left shoulder, its capacitor screaming as it unleashes a freezing beam point-blank into my spine.

Frost coats my coat in an instant, biting deep into my flesh like needles. My hardened aura absorbs the worst of the crystallization, preventing my vital organs from freezing solid, though my muscles lock in agony. I grit my teeth, whip my crossbow around, and drive a steel bolt straight through the drone's optic lens. The casing shatters in a hail of frozen copper.

"Barry!" Flower darts in, four orbiting spheres of white-hot flame spiraling around my torso until warmth thaws the frost in my coat. "I've got you!"

Down in the street, Daren waves from a wooden doorway fifty paces away, ushering Kelrim, Leila, and Hadrik inside before slipping past the threshold.

With the shop secured, we pour fire and frost into the remaining swarm until the surviving spheres bank sharply and retreat into the cloud layer.

We glide down to the street cobblestones just as Daren pushes Pete's front door open, satchels secured over his chest plate.

}
#if(v_combat_technique >= 2 || v_aura_hardening < 3) {
"Daren, push for the shop," I call out. "Flower and I are backing them up. That barrier is about to crack."

"Petal and I are airborne!" Flower shouts, twin jets of orange fire flaring from her bare heels.

"Keep your visual on our line!" Daren bellows over the gunfire. "Kelrim is the only one with the street map!"

"Understood!" I yell up to the rooftops. "Melindra! Give me the updraft!"

Melindra flicks her wrist. Rushing wind curls tight beneath my boots, hurling me thirty feet into the sky. I unlimber my crossbow, nocking a heavy quarrel as Flower and I close ranks with Kate's ice platform.

}
#if(v_combat_technique >= 2) {
My combat technique training keeps the aerial melee readable. I anticipate the attack angles of the bronze spheres, ducking under kinetic slugs and leading crossbow shots directly into their propulsion seams. Flower showers the flank in white-hot flame while Kate's icicles spear optics with ruthless precision.

Down the avenue, Daren waves from the threshold of Pete's shop, pulling Kelrim, Leila, and Hadrik inside.

We hold the air corridor for another thirty seconds until the surviving drones register unsustainable casualties, break formation, and retreat in a high climbing bank.

We drop to the flagstones as Daren and Hadrik emerge with full satchels.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening < 3 && v_combat_technique < 2) {
The swarm overwhelms our defensive perimeter. A bronze sphere drops from a blind angle above my left shoulder, discharging a concentrated freeze ray directly into my back.

Glacial frost encases my torso in a heartbeat. Ice crystals rip through my lungs and freeze the blood in my veins. I catch a blurred glimpse of Flower diving toward me with open palms of flame, but the cold reaches my heart first. The light snaps out.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06a-Entrance, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06a-Entrance) if (v_aura_hardening >= 3 || v_combat_technique >= 2)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_aura_hardening < 3 && v_combat_technique < 2)
